MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I am running a shiny app (https://claney.shinyapps.io/dataAvailabilityApp/) within an iFrame on a Drupal page (http://neoninc.org/data-resources/get-data/data-product-availability).

There are three pre-populated drop downs that filter the data that are used to dynamically generate a chart (ggplot). In all browsers and systems we have tried so far, the app works fine using the direct URL at shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>. And in Safari on a MacBook Pro, the chart loads automatically with the pre-populated values.

However, other PC users using Chrome or Firefox, the chart does not load until a user 'nudges' the app by changing the selection in one of the drop down boxes. Is this a bug with shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>?

Thanks!
Christine

